{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Normal Equation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Normal Equation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"normal equation normal equation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Normal Equation.md","fileName":"Normal Equation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Normal Equation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 19:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Least Squares Methods]] · [[Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Least Squares Methods","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","QR Decomposition","Singular Value Decomposition","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Normal Equation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Normal Equation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"normal equation normal equation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Normal Equation.md","fileName":"Normal Equation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Normal Equation","heading":"Normal Equation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For a least squares problem $Ax\\approx b$, the normal equation is $A^TA\\hat x=A^Tb$. It expresses that the residual $b-A\\hat x$ is orthogonal to every column of $A$.\n\nIf the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the equation has the unique solution $(A^TA)^{-1}A^Tb$. Forming $A^TA$ can worsen conditioning, so [[QR Decomposition]] or [[Singular Value Decomposition]] may be more stable.\n\nFor the source's linear-model notation, the equation is $X^T X\\hat\\beta=X^T Y$. It explains the mathematics behind R's `lm` result while also showing why production implementations do not need to form the displayed inverse directly.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Least Squares Methods","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","QR Decomposition","Singular Value Decomposition","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Normal Equation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Normal Equation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"normal equation normal equation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Normal Equation.md","fileName":"Normal Equation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Normal Equation","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Least Squares Methods","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","QR Decomposition","Singular Value Decomposition","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}